msgstr "Уваход у праграму {PRODUCT_NAME} не выкананы. Гэту ўкладку можна закрыць."

#. Report flow: body of the final screen after a report was sent. {productName} is the name of the app. The second sentence promises the reported person is not told who reported them.
#: src/features/moderation/components/report_flow/ReportFlowCopy.ts
msgid "The {productName} safety team will review your report. We won't reveal that it came from you."
msgstr "Каманда бяспекі {productName} разгледзіць вашу скаргу. Мы не раскрыем, што яна ад вас."

#. Description text in the FluxerTag change modal.
#: src/features/user/components/modals/FluxerTagChangeModal.tsx
msgid "The #0000 tag is reserved for Visionary subscribers. Visionary is no longer available for purchase."
msgstr "Тэг #0000 зарэзерваваны для падпісчыкаў Visionary. Visionary больш нельга купіць."

#. Sentence after the line that starts with By paying in the Operator Pass checkout dialog on an instance that links no privacy policy. The linked text names the Operator Pass privacy notice, which covers the certificate name, the checkout record and the name and avatar people send for the Operators' wall. People never agree to it, it only informs. {OPERATOR_PASS_NAME} is a product name and stays untranslated. Capitalize the linked text the way your language does at its position in the sentence.
#: src/features/app/components/dialogs/components/PurchaseDisclaimer.tsx
msgid "The <0>{OPERATOR_PASS_NAME} privacy notice</0> explains how we handle your data."
msgstr "<0>Паведамленне пра прыватнасць {OPERATOR_PASS_NAME}</0> тлумачыць, як мы абыходзімся з вашымі данымі."

#. Sentence after the line that starts with By paying in the Operator Pass checkout dialog. Both linked texts name legal documents: the privacy policy and the Operator Pass privacy notice, which covers the certificate name, the checkout record and the name and avatar people send for the Operators' wall. People never agree to either, they only inform. {OPERATOR_PASS_NAME} is a product name and stays untranslated. Capitalize the linked texts the way your language does at their position in the sentence.
#: src/features/app/components/dialogs/components/PurchaseDisclaimer.tsx
msgid "The <0>privacy policy</0> and the <1>{OPERATOR_PASS_NAME} privacy notice</1> explain how we handle your data."
msgstr "<0>Палітыка прыватнасці</0> і <1>паведамленне пра прыватнасць {OPERATOR_PASS_NAME}</1> тлумачаць, як мы абыходзімся з вашымі данымі."

#. Notice right above the Create account button when the instance only has a privacy policy. It only informs, people never agree to it.
#: src/features/auth/flow/RegistrationLegalNotice.tsx
msgid "The <0>privacy policy</0> explains how we handle your data."
msgstr "<0>Палітыка прыватнасці</0> тлумачыць, як мы абыходзімся з вашымі данымі."

#. Report flow: body of the final screen after a report was sent, on a self-hosted instance whose own administrators handle reports. The second sentence promises the reported person is not told who reported them.
#: src/features/moderation/components/report_flow/ReportFlowCopy.ts
msgid "The administrators of this instance will review your report. We won't reveal that it came from you."
msgstr "Адміністратары гэтага экзэмпляра разгледзяць вашу скаргу. Мы не раскрыем, што яна ад вас."

#. Error shown when the setup wizard cannot load because the API origin differs from the page origin.
#: src/features/app/components/setup/SelfHostedSetupWizardGate.tsx
msgid "The API is on a different origin than this page, so setup requests are sent without your session. Check the public origin and port this instance is configured with, then reload."
msgstr "API знаходзіцца на іншай крыніцы (origin), чым гэта старонка, таму запыты наладкі адпраўляюцца без вашага сеанса. Праверце публічную крыніцу і порт, з якімі наладжаны гэты экзэмпляр, а потым перазагрузіце старонку."

#: src/features/app/components/ErrorFallback.tsx
msgid "The app crashed"
msgstr "Праграма аварыйна завяршылася"

#: src/features/app/components/ErrorFallback.tsx
msgid "The app has crashed. Checking for updates that might fix this issue…"
msgstr "Праграма аварыйна завяршылася. Правяраем абнаўленні, якія могуць выправіць гэту праблему…"

#. Text under the heading The Operator badge on a slide in the Operator Pass checkout dialog. The quoted example is the text on the badge, translate it the way the app shows it in your language. Operator badge is a name, keep Operator in English. Never add a word that says how long the badge lasts.
#: src/features/premium/components/operator_pass/checkout/OperatorPassShowcaseSlides.ts
msgid "The badge on your Fluxer profile shows when you got your pass, like \"Operator Pass since November 2026\". You can hide it, or just its date, in your settings at any time."
msgstr "Бэйдж у вашым профілі Fluxer паказвае, калі вы атрымалі пропуск, напрыклад «Operator Pass з лістапада 2026». Схаваць яго або толькі дату можна ў наладах у любы час."

#. Activity log detail line under a lifted ban, for a temporary ban that had already ended on its own before it was lifted. A ban is the community ban, not the feature that blocks a user. {date} is when the ban ended, shown as a formatted date and time.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "The ban had already expired on {date}"
msgstr "Тэрмін бану ўжо скончыўся {date}"

